# NOVA: Preliminary Protocol-X Transfer Experiment

## Summary
In a preliminary synthetic transfer experiment, the learned-skill condition achieved 5/5 verified successes, compared with 3/5 for the no-memory condition. The learned-skill condition used 3 agent-loop steps per run; successful no-memory runs averaged 5 steps. The sample is small (n=5), the success-rate difference is not statistically significant (p=0.22), and the causes of the two baseline failures require further investigation. These results motivate larger, controlled evaluations of procedural extraction and transfer.

## What this experiment actually tests
The acquisition task (`parcel_pipe`) explicitly presented the "Protocol-X" rule in its docstring. Therefore, this experiment tests whether NOVA can **extract an instructed procedure from a verified trace and transfer it to a new domain**, not whether it can autonomously discover a hidden rule.

